{
    "name": "Riverflow",
    "version": "19.0.1.1334",  # 19.0.1.1334: a transition can refuse while open services remain (radar pipeline applicants plan, decisions 145-147). New riverflow.transition.refuse_with_open_services: the transition wizard's save check refuses with an error that names the open services below the record; services the transition closes by itself do not count (the marked transitions of execute_child_transitions, cancel_children, auto_done_children_on_enter). riverflow.state.mixin gets one meaning of child services for any record with a workflow (_workflow_child_services: for a service its child services, for another record the services whose subject it is), _execute_child_transitions moves to the mixin so the walk of Q162 also runs for an employee, log entry or ship, and _open_services_left_by mirrors the walk with the shared helper _closing_transition_for. No migration. Tests: test_execute_child_transitions.  # 19.0.1.1332: riverflow.state._put_fixed_open_tasks_on_rule(only=None) takes the services to reset (radar pipeline applicants plan, decision 161, revising Q157): a fixed date can be a date a person typed on purpose, so a migration names the tasks whose fixed date came by accident; with only, the method changes only those, while they are still open, in the state and on Self. No migration. Test: test_state_deadline_on_entry (test_only_resets_the_named_tasks).  # 19.0.1.1331: a copied template note is dated at the copy, by OdooBot, with the first line "From the service template" (radar pipeline applicants plan, decision 160). _create_service_member_from_template kept the template note's author, create_uid and date, so a service made today showed the note as an old note of its author (Ries, 6-Oct-2025 on every new work permit service). The template note does not change. No migration here (the radar migration crewradar_cuneus_sign 19.0.6.245 gives the copies on open work permit services the same shape). Test: test_template_note_copy.  # 19.0.1.1328: the confirmation "I confirm — save with these warnings" is the footer of the yellow box: checkbox first, label across both columns, in the colours of .alert-warning (radar pipeline applicants plan, decision 154; Q138 (a): Fred read the first OK on Cancel Offboarding as "the OK button does not work"). New static/src/components/save_check/save_check_field.scss selects the row by field name, so every form with the save check group gets it; no view or Python change. No migration.  # 19.0.1.1324: the save check box shows two or more findings of one level as a numbered list, one finding as a plain line (Ries, 10-Oct-2026; static/src/components/save_check/save_check_field.xml). No migration. Test: hoot save_check.test.js.  # 19.0.1.1321: a state that ends the case closes the child services that are not started through their own transition (radar pipeline applicants plan, Q162; Ries 10-Oct-2026). New riverflow.state.execute_child_transitions (the parent service decides WHEN) and riverflow.transition.execute_on_parent_transitions (the child service's workflow decides HOW), one shared Selection with the named value "cancel". riverflow.service._execute_child_transitions walks the tree below a service in such a state: an open child service whose state has a marked transition executes it through its own transition wizard (_execute_transition_in_code opens and saves it with a replaced context, as the bot does), a closed one is descended through, a started one stays open with its child services. The transition wizard calls it after the two cascades; code that writes such a state calls it itself. The Cancel transitions of Task, Taxi Supply Order and Train Ticket and the Not Needed transition of Send Email carry "cancel"; no riverflow state sets it. Post-migrate marks the four noupdate transitions. Tests: test_execute_child_transitions.  # 19.0.1.1317: the moved kanban card is shown and tinted (radar plan crewradar-hr/plans/kanban-moved-card.md, Ries 9-Oct-2026). New static/src/patch/kanban_record_patch.js adds the row-bg-{highlight_row_type} class of list_renderer_patch.js to a kanban card whose highlight_row is true, so a card a user changed in the last 10 seconds gets the light blue tint of a changed list row on every board that loads the two fields; static/src/scss/bg-decorations.scss lays the tint over the card's own background ($o-view-background-color), because the list's transparent tint replaced it and was invisible on a dark board. kanban_renderer_patch.js: after the step screen of a drop closes and the board reloads, riverflowPinMovedCards puts the cards moved on this board first in their columns until the page is refreshed, the latest on top (riverflowMovedIds on the renderer); a moved card the reload did not load (a long column; the radar boards load 80 cards a page) is read with one search_read in the board's search and added on top (addExistingRecord, its count raise undone); after Discard nothing is put first; the board scrolls to the card (onPatched, scrollIntoView "nearest"). No migration. Tests: test_kanban_drop (the step flags the record), hoot kanban_drop.test.js (tint, first in the column beyond the loaded page, the next drop on top, Discard).  19.0.1.1316: a state carries a deadline setting (radar pipeline applicants plan, release R5c): riverflow.state.deadline_on_entry (keep, rule with deadline_rule_from and deadline_days, follow-up, today, no deadline). Every step into the state applies it unless the step names its own deadline key or the user chooses a deadline on the step screen; the task step screen proposes it; a task made on a start step takes it. "Keep" is the default, so a state without a setting behaves as before. No migration here.  # 19.0.1.1311: a kanban drop is a step (radar pipeline applicants plan, decision 127). On a board grouped by state_id to riverflow.state, a card dropped in another column no longer writes the state: static/src/patch/kanban_renderer_patch.js calls the new riverflow.state.mixin.action_kanban_drop(from_state_id, to_state_id), which opens the step screen of the first transition on the record's button strip (by sequence) into that column, refuses a card whose state changed since the board loaded, and answers a warning notice that names the steps on offer when none leads there. The radar Employees board wrote the state directly, so the step's work (a started contract, an agreement date) was skipped. No migration. Tests: test_kanban_drop, hoot kanban_drop.test.js.  # 19.0.1.1309: animation frames for a hidden page on a local server (static/src/core/hidden_page_animation_frames.js, prepended to web._assets_core before owl.js): on localhost a hidden page falls back from requestAnimationFrame to a 16 ms timer, so OWL keeps drawing when the agent's browser pane is hidden; production is never served from localhost and keeps the browser's behaviour (radar pipeline applicants plan, R5 follow-up, Ries 9-Oct-2026). # 19.0.1.1302: one open service per subject (radar pipeline applicants plan, release R2, decisions 66, 87, 89). New unique index riverflow_service_single_open_uniq on (workflow_id, res_model, res_id) WHERE is_open AND workflow_enforce_single_open, a stored related of workflow_id.enforce_single_open; it replaces the hand-written work permit index of crewradar_cuneus_sign and covers every workflow with the flag (the flag is now on the workflow form). The auto-add creates services from a clean context (clean_context, then its own defaults): a step screen passed its default_* values, so a new task copied the due date of the task whose step saved a permit (radar service 37725). The start-service wizard keeps only the subject and parent keys and gives the typed date to the started service only; its sub-services took the typed date as well. A manual archive or delete of an open task on a single-open workflow runs the auto-add again for its subject and sends the user a notification: the task comes back, and the steps into a cancelled end state stop it. _single_open_removal_blocked still refuses both for a started task or a task with a live sub-task. No migration: Odoo builds the column and the index on -u (a duplicate open service stops the upgrade; production has none). Tests: test_single_open_workflow.  # 19.0.1.1301: browser tour riverflow_team_form_opens (web.assets_tests, excluded from web.assets_unit_tests) opens a team from the team list as an admin and as a non-admin; it caught the team form hang fixed in oteny_shortcut 19.0.1.246 (Thijs 2026-10-07). Tests: test_team_channel_copy TestTeamFormOpens.  # 19.0.1.1300: an info service of a supply order leg is due on the order's supply date (supply_actual_date, else deadline), the date crewradar's passenger compute also writes; it was due on the order's deadline, so the two computes flipped the value on every recompute (Ries, 8-Oct-2026; radar plan tombstones-instead-of-deletes-in-computes, finding F3). _compute_project_deadline reads the two order fields as _compute_supply_date defines them: one more computed hop through supply_date overflowed the stack in the nested recompute of credential services. No migration: the next recompute corrects a stored value.  # 19.0.1.1299: no compute deletes a record any more (radar plan tombstones-instead-of-deletes-in-computes). New abstract model riverflow.tombstone.mixin (models/riverflow_tombstone_mixin.py): _retire() writes to_be_deleted True and active False in one write (no flush, no cache clear), clears the stored non-computed ondelete set-null Many2one links to the records, retires the ondelete-cascade children that also use the mixin, and registers one pre-commit step (_tombstone_purge) that deletes the flagged rows and flushes; @api.autovacuum _gc_tombstones is the fallback; init() sets the column defaults; the mixin active is read-only in the UI (no Archive action); the retire write disables chatter tracking (the commit deletes the record). T1: riverflow.check.result inherits it; _sync_check_results skips flagged rows and retires instead of unlink(); the service check-result scope search filters the flag. T5: riverflow.service inherits it (its own active stays writable, readonly=False): a retire is not a manual archive (the write guard skips it), the unlink guards skip flagged rows (the commit step deletes what a compute removed), display_order reads siblings without flagged rows (SQL AND NOT to_be_deleted), and the auto-add dedup does not count a retired service as a handled occasion. Perf (radar billing month move 650,067 -> 41,187 queries, log entry date change 1749 -> 934, on the production copy): new riverflow.service._write_changed(vals) writes only the values that differ (a write of unchanged values still runs the dependency searches and the state hooks); _compute_project_deadline and _compute_display_name assign use_project_deadline_from and name only on a change; assign_sequence stores a pending sibling's display_order under protection instead of a write per sibling; riverflow.state.record._compute_tag_ids assigns only changed tags. Test: test_service_write_changed. No migration: active and to_be_deleted are new columns (Odoo writes active True on existing rows, init() sets to_be_deleted false). Tests: test_tombstone_mixin.  # 19.0.1.1294: check results on a service (radar plan cuneus_barney/plans/service-check-results-in-riverflow.md). riverflow.check.result.service_id, routed to the service's Radar row in _compute_state_record_id; riverflow.service gets riverflow.check.results.mixin and a stored check_result_ids (models/riverflow_service_check_results.py) shown as Issue tags on the service form. An app produces checks through three hooks (_get_services_with_checks, _get_service_check_types, _get_service_check_results); a service no producer claims costs nothing. Base depends: active and state_id.is_end_state; a producer adds narrow depends of its own. The compute skips while the registry loads. First producer: crewradar_creds placement_already_covered. No migration. Tests: test_service_check_results.  # 19.0.1.1288: save check (riverflow.save.check.mixin, plan radar plans/save-check.md). Every transition wizard gets save_check_state, save_check_findings and save_check_confirmed; _register_hook wraps action_save on the final registry class so _save_check() runs before every override; a hold returns the client action riverflow_save_check_hold (the dialog stays open and reloads) and bot_claim answers it as ok False. First consumer: the incomplete-children warning of riverflow.service.wizard (incomplete_children_warning and ignore_incomplete_children are gone). The transition wizard forms that do not inherit the root view carry the three view lines. No migration: transient rows are vacuumed and -u drops the removed columns. Tests: test_save_check, hoot save_check.test.js.  # 19.0.1.1285: the Named Domain form's domain widget sets allow_expressions, so a domain that calls datetime.date.today() no longer shows "Invalid domain" and counts its records. Test: test_named_domain_form_allows_expressions.  # 19.0.1.1284: riverflow.service.template_service_id remembers the template a service was cloned from (set in _create_service_member_from_template). _create_deferred_children finds the template through that link first and dedups a deferred child by it: the email step renames a child to the email subject, so the name match created duplicates when a parent came back to the state. A child in a cancelled state no longer blocks a fresh clone. New transition context key cancel_children cancels the open subtree after the state write, before the deferred children run. No migration: a new nullable column; services from before the link fall back to the name.  # 19.0.1.1281: a bounced outgoing email opens one Review email bounce task (template riverflow.template_service_review_email_bounce, Task workflow, Not started). One open child per bounced mail.message; a later notification on that message appends the address to the same internal note. The hook is mail.thread._routing_handle_bounce, after the bounce write, so the temporary exception from mail.mail._send does not open a task. Archiving the template, or removing its xmlid, turns it off and leaves an open child as it is. Post-migrate backfills a bounce whose mail.message.date is within 72 hours, and only when that message is the latest email on the record. Tests: test_review_email_bounce.  # 19.0.1.1275: colleague message copy (Thijs 2026-09-28). A staff user's chatter message to a staff member of ANOTHER team is also posted in that colleague's home team Discuss channel, so a request to one person no longer stays in one mailbox (staff are on "Handle by Emails"). New res.users.home_team_id and the riverflow.team Members list (member_ids, the One2many side, on the team form); a mail.thread._message_create hook (models/mail_thread.py) on every record with a chatter covers Send message, a Log note @mention, the Email Sender Wizard and a staff email reply; only between teams, never to the sender, one copy per team, a team contact as recipient counts. The external message copy of the review mixin is unchanged. No migration: a new nullable column, members are set by hand. Rules: skills riverflow/references/team-channels.md. Tests: test_team_channel_copy.  # 19.0.1.1274: riverflow.auto.add.domain is renamed to the generic riverflow.named.domain (Named Domains): the auto-add rules and the crewradar salary auto-add components already use it, and rivercreds now points credential type groups to it for their applicability (Thijs 2026-09-28). The pre-migrate renames the table, sequence, constraints and indexes, the model-name references (ir_model, ir_model_fields model/relation, ir_model_data.model of every module, action, views, filters) and riverflow's own XML ids, so rows, ids and XML ids survive and no column is dropped. The form lists the auto-add rules that use a domain. The state form shows counts_as_active_employment and requires_onboarding_credentials, which credential planning reads and which were set in data only. # 19.0.1.1265: StateRecordCalendarController extends Odoo's CalendarController again and the state record list drops js_class="shortcut_list": the shortcut banner now comes from oteny_shortcut's Layout on every view (Thijs 2026-09-14).  # 19.0.1.1257: a person may take ONE exit out from under a live bot run — the state's is_bot_timeout hand-back, which is the exit the timeout reaper already takes on that same record once the SLA passes. Taking it early is the same judgement the clock makes on an abandoned run, and it lands in the same state, so it is one hand-back with two triggers rather than a second meaning; every other exit, Cancel above all, stays refused while the run is live. Before this, a run whose gateway died held the record in-progress and the SLA was the only door, which parks a person in front of a bot that will never answer. The submit race the fence was built for is fenced closer to the act than this method can reach: the agent re-checks its epoch (bot_token_check) immediately before the irreversible call, and the hand-back clears bot_claim_token in the same transaction as the state change. New riverflow.state.bot_timeout_transition() is the one lookup the reaper and the fence share. transition_buttons_json now renders that abort under the working note instead of hiding every button, so the panel that says "handed back at HH:MM" also offers the door; the button dict moved into _transition_button() so both branches build the same shape. Tests: test_mfnl_concurrency TestHumanTransitionGuard, test_transition_buttons_bot_hide, test_mfnl_one_live_run drain. No data migration here; the client module writes its own button text.  # 19.0.1.1251: auto_add_services occasion dedup ignores CLOSED services (end state or archived) on a workflow with enforce_single_open — only an open service blocks a candidate, and _filter_single_open already dedups on open-ness. The presence side of the single-open golden rule says an in-scope subject always holds one open service; a Done task for the current occasion used to count as handled, so HR filing the passport already on file through Renew Passport (importer attached the scan to the existing passport, wizard closed the task) left the employee with no open task and deleting the Done task did not bring one back (10-Sep-2026, Saw Armstrong on test2; reproduced on crmain). Also reaches Arrange Work Permit by decision. Workflows without single-open keep the full dedup (hand-in services keyed on one card). Test: test_closed_service_blocks_only_without_single_open. No data migration — existing victims are healed by hand.  # 19.0.1.1249: timeline/layout_range.js — shortcut layout ⇄ timeline window (layoutFromRange / rangeParamsFromLayout: a scale means its default window around today; a custom period is fixed dates or relative_period in whole months), with hoot tests. timeline/range_persistence.js and its tests are removed: the planning views no longer store their range in localStorage.  # 19.0.1.1241: many2many_binary uploads block the UI until the file is linked, and a late upload into a closed dialog warns instead of crashing with "Component is destroyed" (many2many_binary_upload_patch.js).  # 19.0.1.1238: refuse a transition wizard that cannot carry the record.  # 19.0.1.1237: public prepare_transition_action for /json/2/.  # 19.0.1.1236: strip extras, wizard door, set_deadline_relative, bot_claim runs the wizard.  # 19.0.1.1224: working-note clocks use the viewing user's timezone.  # 19.0.1.1218: occupant-of-workflow + queued search for the operator UI.  # 19.0.1.1217: drain resumes a fresh SLA-less login park; bot_token_check accepts work_token-only.  # 19.0.1.1216: a SLA-less login park does not occupy the one-live-slot.  # 19.0.1.1215: hide claim/work from HR; no primary on bot queue/fill; live claim shows a working note; queue SLA reaper.  # 19.0.1.1203: bot_login_hold on riverflow.state + one-live-slot drain  # 19.0.1.1201: cancel cascade. `auto_done_children_on_enter` on a state that is ALSO `is_cancelled_state` now cancels the children instead of completing them, and walks the FULL subtree rather than the direct children only (`_cascade_cancel_to_subtree` / `_cancel_end_state`). Both differences are what cancelling actually means: closing a taxi that was never taken as "Done" reads as work completed, and a cancelled parent typically sits above a marker child that is already Done while the bookings under THAT marker are still open — those bookings are exactly what has to be dropped, so an already-finished node is descended through instead of stopping the walk. Workflows without a cancelled state fall back to their first normal end state. Behaviour-neutral for every existing user of the flag: no shipped cancelled state carries it (AUV deliberately does not cascade). Fallback for a workflow WITHOUT a cancelled state is now its LAST end state by sequence, not its first: workflows here are sequenced "work finished" before "no work happened" (Done 30 -> Not Needed 40 -> Cancelled 50), so the last one is the closest thing to a cancel on offer (Send Email lands on Not Needed instead of Done). The generic Task workflow gained a hidden `state_task_cancelled` end state + Cancel buttons on Not started / In Progress and a Re-start off it -- it had only Done, so a called-off task (the AB Appointment marker above all) could only be closed as work completed. First consumer: the work permit Cancelled state, crewradar_cuneus_sign 19.0.5.62.  # 19.0.1.1200: dropped the now-vestigial `model` / `subjects` parameters from _filter_single_open. Since the single-open guard started looking existing open services up per CANDIDATE res_model (so subject-redirected candidates are checked against their actual subject, not the trigger model), neither argument was read anywhere in the body. Sole call site updated; no behaviour change.  # 19.0.1.1198: workflow cleanup + icon fix (icon-audit 2026-08-10, usage checked on crmain). Send Notification fa-envelope -> fa-bell (Send Email owns the envelope; both sit side by side in the picker, the bell marks the one-shot variant; noupdate=1 file -> migration pushes it, guarded on the shipped value). RETIRED the "To Be Invoiced" workflow stub: never went live (zero services on crmain, transitions never uncommented) and its fa-file-invoice-dollar icon was FA5-only — Odoo ships FontAwesome 4.7, so it rendered as an EMPTY box; XML file removed, migration deletes the noupdate rows (guarded: skips if services exist). Migration also archives the hand-made "AB Appointment (Do not use, work in progress)" workflow found on crmain (UI-created, no xml id, zero services — superseded by the real Arrange Work Permit workflow; matched by exact name + no-xmlid + no-usage). New tests/test_workflow_icons.py validates EVERY riverflow.workflow/transition/transition-action icon class against the FA 4.7 css shipped with Odoo, so FA5-only names can no longer slip in unnoticed.  # 19.0.1.1196: auto-add engine — candidate-aware dedup + single-open guard. Filter hooks may REDIRECT candidates to a different subject than the trigger model (rivercreds credential-subject rules anchor the service on the credential's holder); the dedup and open-service lookups now group candidates by their own res_model and key on (rule, res_model, res_id, context_ref) instead of searching only the trigger model, so redirected candidates no longer escape dedup on re-evaluation. Behaviour-neutral when no hook rewrote candidates.  # 19.0.1.1182: WP renewal waiver (Phase C / R1+R5a) — generic delete/archive guard on riverflow.service: `_single_open_removal_blocked()` refuses unlink (and manual archive) of an `is_open` service on an `enforce_single_open` workflow that is past its initial state OR still has live (active, non-end-state) child services. A childless initial-state monitoring service stays removable (self-heals in crewradar_creds). See rivercreds/references/golden-rules-and-waivers.md R1.
    "depends": ["base", "mail", "documents", "oteny_shortcut", "oteny_bot"],
    "author": "Vriend Studio",
    "category": "Workflow",
    "description": """
    Task manager for the Service Industry
    """,
    # data files always loaded at installation
    "data": [
        "security/riverflow_security.xml",
        "security/ir.model.access.csv",
        "data/riverflow_teams_data.xml",
        "wizards/riverflow_transition_wizard_view.xml",
        "wizards/riverflow_service_wizard_view.xml",
        "wizards/riverflow_start_service_view.xml",
        "wizards/riverflow_service_email_sender_view.xml",
        "wizards/riverflow_service_register_wizard_view.xml",
        "wizards/riverflow_supplier_confirmed_view.xml",
        "wizards/riverflow_enter_train_ticket_view.xml",
        "wizards/riverflow_enter_airline_ticket_view.xml",
        "wizards/riverflow_enter_distance_wizard_view.xml",
        "wizards/riverflow_set_deadline_tomorrow_wizard_view.xml",
        "wizards/riverflow_verify_trip_locations_wizard_view.xml",
        "views/riverflow_service_views.xml",
        "views/riverflow_workflow_views.xml",
        "views/riverflow_state_views.xml",
        "views/riverflow_transition_views.xml",
        "views/riverflow_transition_action_views.xml",
        "views/riverflow_state_record_views.xml",
        "views/riverflow_team_views.xml",
        "views/riverflow_named_domain_views.xml",
        "views/riverflow_auto_add_service_views.xml",
        "views/riverflow_check_result_views.xml",
        "views/res_config_settings_views.xml",
        "data/transition_action_data.xml",
        "data/workflow_service_task.xml",
        "data/service_review_email_bounce_template.xml",
        "data/service_email_workflow.xml",
        "data/service_send_notification_workflow.xml",
        "data/service_arrange_and_send_workflow.xml",
        # "data/riverflow_back_office_workflow.xml",
        "data/riverflow_taxi_order_workflow.xml",
        "data/riverflow_taxi_leg_workflow.xml",
        "data/riverflow_train_ticket_workflow.xml",
        "data/ir_config_parameter_data.xml",
        "data/riverflow_bot_cron.xml",
    ],
    "assets": {
        # Before owl.js, which captures requestAnimationFrame when it loads: on a
        # local development server a hidden page keeps drawing (see the file).
        "web._assets_core": [
            ("prepend", "riverflow/static/src/core/hidden_page_animation_frames.js"),
        ],
        "web.assets_backend": [
            "riverflow/static/src/components/**/*",
            # Dark mode files load via web.assets_web_dark only
            (
                "remove",
                "riverflow/static/src/components/timeline/timeline_scale_selector.dark.scss",
            ),
            "riverflow/static/src/patch/**/*",
            "riverflow/static/src/riverflow_force_xl.js",
            "riverflow/static/src/scss/bg-decorations.scss",
        ],
        "web.assets_web_dark": [
            "riverflow/static/src/components/timeline/timeline_scale_selector.dark.scss",
        ],
        "web.assets_unit_tests": [
            "riverflow/static/tests/**/*",
            ("remove", "riverflow/static/tests/tours/**/*"),
        ],
        "web.assets_tests": [
            "riverflow/static/tests/tours/**/*",
        ],
    },
    "application": True,
    "auto_install": False,
    "license": "OEEL-1",
}
